# Mask x on =dev-libs/slotusetarget-2.0 only (versioned atom, bare flag
# syntax -- package.use.mask exists at repo/profile level, never user
# config): autounmask must not flip x on for 2.0 to satisfy
# >=dev-libs/slotusetarget-1.0[x], so the slot conflict between 1.0
# (x on) and 2.0 (x off, unflippable) survives to the notice renderer:
# [y] reports a missing-IUSE (unconditional) key, [x] a violated key.
# 1.0 keeps its +x default (unmasked), so slotusex still pulls it.
=dev-libs/slotusetarget-2.0 x
